# Intake Layer

This layer answers: "Which materials are allowed into {{REPO_NAME}}, and what will they be used for?"

Intake only registers owner-approved material entrypoints, intended use, visibility, processing state, and banned boundaries. Raw private text, secrets, tokens, customer material, and unauthorized personal material must not be written here.

## Recommended Records

- Material entrypoint: local path, external system, memory wiki, public link, or human summary.
- Intended use: Wenxin, PSP, IPO Reverse, Taste Generator, runtime session, capability review, or work context.
- Boundary: public, private collaboration, local/server authority, or banned material.
- State: pending, approved, processed, rejected, or archived.

Stable facts move to memory or identity; reusable procedures move to capabilities or runtime skills; reviewable lessons move to evolution.
